  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(c) The probability of showing same number by both dice $p=\\frac{6}{36}=\\frac{1}{6}$\r\nIn binomial distribution here $n=4, r=2, p=$\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\frac{1}{6}, \\mathrm{q}=\\frac{5}{6} \\\\\r\n\\text { req. probability }={ }^{n} C_{r} q^{n-r} p^{r}={ }^{4} C_{2}\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^{2} \\\\\r\n=6\\left(\\frac{25}{36}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{36}\\right)=\\frac{25}{216}\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
